{"path":"concepts/signed_integral","title":"std::signed_integral","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>signed_integral","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/concepts/signed_integral","section":"concepts","kind":"page","summary":"The concept signed_integral<T> is satisfied if and only if T is an integral type and std::is_signed_v<T> is true.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/concepts\">&lt;concepts&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>concept signed_integral <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/integral\"><span class=\"kw2956\">std::<span class=\"me2\">integral</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_signed\"><span class=\"kw524\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_signed_v</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The concept <code>signed_integral&lt;T&gt;</code> is satisfied if and only if <code>T</code> is an integral type and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_signed\"><span class=\"kw524\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_signed_v</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p><code>signed_integral&lt;T&gt;</code> may be satisfied by a type that is not a <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/type#Type_classification\">signed integer type</a>, for example, <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">char</span></span> (on a system where <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">char</span></span> is signed).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;concepts&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string_view&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">void</span> test<span class=\"br0\">(</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">signed_integral</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> x, <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view\"><span class=\"kw1256\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string_view</span></span></a> text <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> text <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" (\"</span> <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>text <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> x <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\") is a signed integral<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">void</span> test<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/unsigned_integral\"><span class=\"kw2957\">std::<span class=\"me2\">unsigned_integral</span></span></a> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> x, <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view\"><span class=\"kw1256\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string_view</span></span></a> text <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> text <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" (\"</span> <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>text <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> x <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\") is an unsigned integral<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">void</span> test<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> x, <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view\"><span class=\"kw1256\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string_view</span></span></a> text <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> text <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" (\"</span> <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>text <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> x <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\") is non-integral<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    test<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">42</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>               <span class=\"co1\">// signed</span>\n    test<span class=\"br0\">(</span>0xFULL, <span class=\"st0\">\"0xFULL\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// unsigned</span>\n    test<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">'A'</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>              <span class=\"co1\">// platform-dependent</span>\n    test<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw2\">true</span>, <span class=\"st0\">\"true\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>     <span class=\"co1\">// unsigned</span>\n    test<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu19\">4e-2</span>, <span class=\"st0\">\"4e-2\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>     <span class=\"co1\">// non-integral (hex-float)</span>\n    test<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"∫∫\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>             <span class=\"co1\">// non-integral</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>(42) is a signed integral\n0xFULL (15) is an unsigned integral\n(A) is a signed integral\ntrue (1) is an unsigned integral\n4e-2 (0.04) is non-integral\n(∫∫) is non-integral</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c++23\">\n<ul><li> C++23 standard (ISO/IEC 14882:2024): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 18.4.7 Arithmetic concepts [concepts.arithmetic] \n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c++20\">\n<ul><li> C++20 standard (ISO/IEC 14882:2020): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 18.4.7 Arithmetic concepts [concepts.arithmetic] \n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_integral\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>is_integral</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   checks if a type is an integral type  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_signed\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>is_signed</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   checks if a type is a signed arithmetic type  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"concepts","title":"Concepts library (since C++20)"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::signed_integral","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++20. The concept signed_integral<T> is satisfied if and only if T is an integral type and std::is_signed_v<T> is true."},{"label":"Notes","note":"signed_integral<T> may be satisfied by a type that is not a signed integer type, for example, char (on a system where char is signed)."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"is_integral","note":"checks if a type is an integral type"},{"label":"is_signed","note":"checks if a type is a signed arithmetic type"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++20"],"wordCount":245,"codeBlockCount":2}
